Hi

I've been experiencing an apparently intermittent problem with load_all() and document() appearing to be unhappy with, or happy with my R code, depending on what  had done earlier.

I have finally managed to reproduce what causes the behaviour, and have done so in the sequence of 3 successive editions of the same baby package (collateexample) which I have attached.  Now I know what's happening I can work round it, but I think it is probably not what should be happening, so I'll report my experience here, in the hope it's useful.

The baby package has 3 files (and the names of the files are important to reproducing the behaviour! that's what made it hard to discover in my real project).

file x-code.r defines and documents a generic function (gen1)
file a-code.r defines and documents a method for the gen1.  The @include x-code.r tag is at the top of a-code.r
file y-code.r does nothing at all.  It just contains an @include x-code.r tag as part of a trick to make load_all() and document() happy (eventually).

When I first try to run this I get the following output:

d> load_all()
Loading collateexample
 Show Traceback

 Rerun with Debug
 Error in setMethod("gen1", signature = "numeric", def = function(a) { (from a-code.r#12) :
  no existing definition for function ‘gen1’
d>

This version of the code is in collateexample.1.zip.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If however I remove a-code.r (or just rename it temporarily to a-code.r.old)

I can then successfully run load_all() and document().

document()
Updating collateexample documentation
Loading collateexample
First time using roxygen2 4.0. Upgrading automatically...
